than the graveyard from the battlefield. For example, if a permanent with a finality counter on it would be put into its owner's hand from the battlefield, it does so normally.","oracle_id":"3dee768a-612c-4960-bad2-2fe5b83a70c3","published_at":"2025-06-06","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Finality counters work on any permanent, not only creatures. If a permanent with a finality counter on it would be put into a graveyard from the battlefield, exile it instead.","oracle_id":"3dee768a-612c-4960-bad2-2fe5b83a70c3","published_at":"2025-06-06","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"Multiple finality counters on a single permanent are redundant.","oracle_id":"3dee768a-612c-4960-bad2-2fe5b83a70c3","published_at":"2025-06-06","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.","oracle_id":"8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90","published_at":"2012-07-01","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This is not modal. If the target changes from an artifact to an enchantment or vice versa, this still destroys it.","oracle_id":"a7e97fa9-4b72-4548-b854-5be5f18a6f1a","published_at":"2004-10-04","source":"wotc"},{"comment":"This has no effect on those permanents other than letting them interact with things that care about enchantments.","oracle_id":"c56ea5ce-c8de-46c2-a8dd-bdd41467a28c","published_at":"2008-05-01","source":"wotc"}],"schema_version":1,"source":"Scryfall Oracle/rulings subset for offline tests"}
